[
    {
        "content": "<p>Would a small API addition after <code>FiniteField.frobenius_pow</code> be welcome in <code>Mathlib/FieldTheory/Finite/Basic.lean</code>?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- Powers of Frobenius may be reduced modulo the extension degree. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">frobenius_pow_eq_pow_mod</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">frobenius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">frobenius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pow_eq_pow_mod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">frobenius_pow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcard</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Pointwise form of `frobenius_pow_eq_pow_mod`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iterateFrobenius_mod</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iterateFrobenius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">iterateFrobenius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">iterateFrobenius_eq_pow</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iterateFrobenius_eq_pow</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">frobenius_pow_eq_pow_mod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>They support endomorphism rewriting and elementwise rewriting.<br>\nAre the names and placement appropriate?</p>",
        "id": 611537750,
        "sender_full_name": "Attila Vajda",
        "timestamp": 1784479318
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For both of them the RHS looks more complex than the LHS (from the point of view of thinking about them as terms in a type theory) which is not normally how we write things in mathlib -- maybe switch the sides of the equalities?</p>",
        "id": 611547614,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1784486800
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this is the direction that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.I_pow_eq_pow_mod#doc\">docs#Complex.I_pow_eq_pow_mod</a> goes, with the mod on the rhs</p>",
        "id": 611547909,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784487072
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>no pun intended</p>",
        "id": 611547980,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784487149
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah it does feel quite natural going that way, it's a bit of a weird one. Not a simp lemma though</p>",
        "id": 611554235,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1784494399
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm we should add a <code>simp</code> lemma for the <code>OfNat</code> case (although <code>norm_num</code> does handle it)</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>(tangent)</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I_pow_ofNat_add_four</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofNat</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">I_pow_eq_pow_mod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">123</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">pow_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 611555907,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1784496150
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39506\">#39506</a></p>",
        "id": 611556061,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784496329
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>nice pattern, thanks for highlighting it!</p>\n<p>I noticed the source theorem <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Basic.html#pow_eq_pow_mod\">pow_eq_pow_mod</a> has this pattern too, with more complex syntax on RHS, but perhaps simpler semantics / normal form (?)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/attilavjda/formal-contributions/blob/main/FrobeniusPeriodicity/CODEBASE_PATTERN_SURVEY.md\">there are other examples, and counterexamples in Mathlib and Lean4 core</a></p>",
        "id": 611631655,
        "sender_full_name": "Attila Vajda",
        "timestamp": 1784542070
    }
